course: dictionary
lesson: 12499
title: Departing and leaving
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Departing» means leaving, going away from a place. You will see it on station boards and timetables, where it tells you when a train, bus or plane sets off.
explain: «The train departing from platform four leaves at nine o'clock.» Departing describes the train that is leaving. The clues are platform four and leaves at nine: the train goes away from the platform at nine.
explain: Departing can also describe a person who is leaving a job or a place. «The departing head teacher gave a speech on her last day.» Her last day tells you she is leaving the school. Try your meaning in the sentence: "the leaving head teacher" still makes sense, so you have got it.
fact: Departing means leaving or going away from a place.
fact: Departing is the -ing form of the verb depart: depart, departs, departed, departing.
fact: «Departures» on a station board shows the trains, buses or planes that are leaving.
fact: «The bus departs at 8:15» means the bus leaves at 8:15.
fact: To find how long a journey takes, subtract the departure time from the arrival time.
exercise: «The train departing from platform four leaves at nine o'clock.» What does departing mean here? | Stopping for a long rest | *Leaving | Covered in paint | Arriving
exercise: The station board says: Bus 12, departs 10:30. What time does the bus leave? | *10:30 | 11:00 | 9:45 | 12:30
exercise: Which word is the -ing form of depart? | departs | depart | departed | *departing
test: «The departing passengers waited by the gate.» What are the passengers doing? | *Leaving through the gate | Buying tickets | Singing | Asleep
test: Ravi reads the board: Train 4, departing 14:05. When does Train 4 leave? | *14:05 | 15:40 | 13:50
exam: Mia's train departs at 7:30 and arrives at 8:15. How long is the journey? | 30 minutes | 55 minutes | *45 minutes | 1 hour
